<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17245" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-splendesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">expl-</span></b> ), dŭi, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to shine forth</i>, <i>glitter</i>
			(rarely before the Aug. period). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 2, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sirius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 12, 12, § 30</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to shine forth</i>,
				<i>be eminent</i>, <i>distinguished</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clarius exsplendescebat, quam condiscipuli
					animo aequo ferre possent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Att. 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporis animique dotes exsplenduerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tit. 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
